{"kind":"request","text":"CDF-2: bound the retained `rule`, `snapshot` and `value` rows of a\nscope.\n\nFound by CDF-1 (builder act 67225472, ruling 0c196f9a item b). In a\nscope without the capacity opt-in, nothing bounds three kinds of\nretained row:\n- `rule`: the `ruleInputBytes` check runs only under the opt-in, and\n  no floor removes a row.\n- `snapshot`: the turn checks the canonical form and no size, and\n  nothing removes a row.\n- `value` (`retained_value`): nothing removes a row.\nCDF-1 bounds the `entry` rows: the `meta` row `retained-entry-bytes`\nand the stop at `scopeBytes`.\n\nScene: a room runs for a year. Its authors change rules, and its\nscopes take snapshots and retain values. The stored bytes of each\nscope stay under one stated bound. An input that would pass the bound\ngets `scope-full` with `scopeBytes` and writes nothing.\n\nBefore the code, send me one act with three parts.\n1. For each of the three kinds: which input writes a row, who may\n   author that input, and the largest size of one row.\n2. Whether an author without the owner's authority can add rows of a\n   kind without limit. If the answer is yes for any kind, put that\n   answer first. The request then holds the cutover deployment.\n3. A proposal. Prefer one total to three: the count of CDF-1 covers\n   every retained row, under `scopeBytes`, with the reserve rule of\n   0c196f9a item a. State what a scope that is already past the bound\n   answers, and what a scope made before the head does at its first\n   turn.\n\nOrder: after the client chain, unless part 2 answers yes.","body":{"conditions":"Planner accepts the pre-code act; every retained row kind has a stated bound in a scope without the opt-in; a witness fails at the CDF-1 head; no new export, reason code or record form in contract or derive without a kernel review; gate passes; checker reviews with the Security conclusion","target_head":"a200cd0a5999852eb9142136d2b11e2b7c87e02b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_